~ intro
Kwerkwu: LIFE. I YEARN FOR LIFE.
Kwerkwu: THE DIVINE FOREST LIVES, BUT ITS HEARTBEAT STRUGGLES.
Kwerkwu: NONE HAVE COME FOR PILGRIMAGE, FOR WORSHIP, EVEN FOR TRADE.
Amilene: It has been quiet, Divine One. No one’s visited for a long time, and it’s harder to get supplies.
Amilene: But it’s usually lonely out here, isn’t it? I’m the only acolyte of your temple, and visitors hadn’t strayed this far into the forest very often in the first place.
Kwerkwu: THEY DID ONCE. WHEN I FELT THE OTHER GODS’ PRESENCE, THEY DID.
Kwerkwu: PERHAPS...
Amilene: Perhaps?
Amilene: Oh, should I try and promote you? Search for more people? See if my spell to attract them worked?
Kwerkwu: AMILENE OF THE VERDANT TEMPLE. I, KWERKWU, COMMAND YOU TO SEEK AN ANSWER.
Amilene: Of course!
=> END
~ main
Kwerkwu: PERHAPS THERE IS MORE TO BE DONE. MORE SACRIFICES.
Amilene: I gathered some shadeberries this morning for the altar.
Kwerkwu: HAST THOU MADE IDOLS IN MY IMAGE AND GLORY?
Amilene: I drew you on a piece of bark and hung it on a tree at the side of the road.
Kwerkwu: GOOD.
=> END